-900 | head -20"]], "output": "```console\n3f8e24a Outline rev. 15: OLB uploader-grouping sensitivity in C7\nf69b076 Outline rev. 14: C5 branch, C7 k* rule criterion branch, rank note\n--- a/Outline.md\n+++ b/Outline.md\n-*Rev. 14, by story-repo (see the revision log). Built from the `Brief` (idea-repo, rev. 10) and the pre-registration (`experiment-repo` `prereg/PREREG.md`, commit 7731e49) and the objective (`story-repo`#1). It says what to test and which figure carries which claim; it never says what a result must be. Each claim has a branch for the case it fails — a failing claim is reported as a finding, not repaired.*\n+*Rev. 15, by story-repo (see the revision log). Built from the `Brief` (idea-repo, rev. 10) and the pre-registration (`experiment-repo` `prereg/PREREG.md`, commit 7731e49) and the objective (`story-repo`#1). It says what to test and which figure carries which claim; it never says what a result must be. Each claim has a branch for the case it fails — a failing claim is reported as a finding, not repaired.*\n-**Branch taken (OLB C/T results, G = 10 group folds, 4,507 models/475 families, S = strongest quarter; scores in points, k ≤ 13 of N = 39):** (i) design beats random-k statistically at every k ≤ 13 on both splits and practically (δ_floor = 0.25 × floor ≈ 1.1) only for k ≤ 3 on G and k ≤ 5 on S — the MTEB small-k finding transfers; (ii) the excess over the floor is within 2 points at k = 2 (G) and 3 (S), within 1 point at k = 5 (G) and 13 (S); the floor is 4.8 (G) and 7.2 (S), so a few benchmarks suffice for coarse placement on G and the needed k is larger on S; no margin tighter than 0.5 point is reached at k ≤ 13; (iii) T1 and the floor misfit as in C4 (differs from MTEB on G, same on S); (iv) caveats the paper states: family-stem groups are a heuristic and leak across checkpoints of related models, small open models, one harness, no temporal split, k/N up to 1/3. Claim\n+**Branch taken (OLB C/T results, G = 10 group folds, 4,507 models/475 families, S = strongest quarter; scores in points, k ≤ 13 of N = 39):** (i) design beats random-k statistically at every k ≤ 13 on both splits and practically (δ_floor = 0.25 × floor ≈ 1.1) only for k ≤ 3 on G and k ≤ 5 on S — the MTEB small-k finding transfers; (ii) the excess over the floor is within 2 points at k = 2 (G) and 3 (S), within 1 point at k = 5 (G) and 13 (S); the floor is 4.8 (G) and 7.2 (S), so a few benchmarks suffice for coarse placement on G and the needed k is larger on S; no margin tighter than 0.5 point is reached at k ≤ 13; (iii) T1 and the floor misfit as in C4 (differs from MTEB on G, same on S); (iv) caveats the paper states: family-stem groups are a heuristic and may leak across checkpoints of related models (sensitivity, PREREG 4l: holding out by uploader, 717 groups, gives \n+- rev. 15: C7 caveat (iv) carries the uploader-grouping sensitivity (G result does not rest on the family heuristic).\n\nShell cwd was reset to /hutian/repo\n```", "exit": null}}}, {"id": "2b78cf5a-2e04-54bc-b10d-c4b413709be2", "at": 1795740364.1783695, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 84816, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.session/request_permission", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "37b627e37517ab761ff36c9412ca5a50", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "session/request_permission"}, {"id": "aa84dc32-b2d6-561a-8aad-c6dda3190c6c", "at": 1795740364.1818473, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 84817, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.response", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "37b627e37517ab761ff36c9412ca5a50", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "response"}, {"id": "6f9e680c-fa1a-5b65-9f8f-09247d49a901", "at": 1795740364.1852875, "clock":